<title>USA: Maine state workers seek amendment on pensions.</title>
<headline>Maine state workers seek amendment on pensions.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Maine State Employees Association, seeking to protect worker pensions, wants a constitutional amendment that would prohibit the state from using pension funds to bail out the Maine budget.</p>
<p>The measure would require lawmakers to appropriate enough funds to ensure that pension benefits are guaranteed. Union members have been collecting thousands of signatures from Maine residents supporting the proposal and plan to submit the petitions to the legislature.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
